---
/**
 * Scroll progress rail — a 3px fill down the leading edge showing how far
 * through the document the reader is. Driven entirely by
 * `animation-timeline: scroll(root)`; no JS, no scroll listener.
 *
 * Hidden outright where scroll-timeline is unsupported (see
 * src/styles/scroll-system.css) rather than left as a dead empty rail.
 *
 * aria-hidden because it duplicates information the scrollbar already gives
 * assistive technology — it is decoration for sighted readers, not a control.
 *
 * Sits immediately after <Nav /> on every page. There is no shared layout
 * component in this project (each page owns its own <html>), so it is added
 * per page rather than inherited.
 */
---

<div class="progress-rail" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
